@!internal
module nupp.runtime.seam.timesuite

--[[
A shape-only suite, like `cryptosuite` and `storagesuite`.

Everything `host.time` promises is the host's, and the provider that answers it
is a browser's, so a vector here would have to reach a browser to assert
anything -- and `stdlibtest` runs these suites with no effects host at all.
`nupp.runtime.seam.module` checks the shape before calling this, which is the
whole of what a loaded module can be held to.

This was the `validate` call the seam's own factory published. The factory is
gone and the check it forwarded to now runs ahead of every suite, so the
forwarding was the only thing left in it.
]]

local suite = {}

@allow("unused-binding")
function suite.test(provider: any): (boolean, string?)
    return true
end

export = suite
